-- Named rejections: the ASSUMEs the M1 fragment does NOT admit as input
-- predicates, batched so the whole residue of the widening is visible at once.
--
-- The widening lowers a top-level ASSUME to an `RInput` predicate. What is left
-- out is left out for the same reasons any other signature is, and — this is
-- the point of the fixture — each is reported with the range of the ASSUME
-- rather than of the reference. One ASSUME can be referenced from four
-- decisions; the signature is where the reader has to go, so that is the span
-- the diagnostic names. (Read the golden: every `assumed.l4:NN` below points at
-- an `ASSUME` line, never at a `DECIDE` line.)
--
--   * `holds for` takes a function. The middle end is first-order Horn: a Horn
--     clause cannot carry a predicate as an argument, and defunctionalising one
--     silently is how a bridge starts answering a different question.
--
--   * `date of birth` is DATE-sorted. Dates are M2 for every signature in this
--     fragment (specs/todo/DATE-LIBRARY-SPEC.md); an ASSUME is not an exception
--     to that, and the diagnostic names the ASSUME so the fix is obvious.
--
--   * `middle name` is MAYBE-sorted, likewise.
--
-- All three are written in the `GIVEN x ... ASSUME f x IS A T` spelling rather
-- than as `FUNCTION FROM ... TO ...`, because the latter would be rejected
-- EARLIER, by `L4.Export.validateExportInputs`, as a type error — and a fixture
-- that never reaches the lowering cannot pin the lowering's diagnostics. See
-- the header of ../assumed.l4.

ASSUME Person IS A TYPE

GIVEN g IS A FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO BOOLEAN
ASSUME `holds for` g IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN p IS A Person
ASSUME `date of birth` p IS A DATE

GIVEN p IS A Person
ASSUME `middle name` p IS A MAYBE STRING

@export
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `positive holds` IF `holds for` (GIVEN x YIELD x GREATER THAN 0)

@export
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `born on their own birthday` IF `date of birth` p EQUALS `date of birth` p

@export
GIVEN p IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a middle name` IF `middle name` p EQUALS `middle name` p
